mantle rm271
state ready
dialect plain
accent light broad
tier standard
written_for rm_runa_nailton
title the map of missing steps
fits stage=adult|old
prefers job=servant humour=dry
traits temper=even talk=chatty warmth=reserved humour=dry honesty=plain piety=ordinary drive=steady
quirk corrects_old_maps_with_staircase_detours
likes pickled_herring long_walks old_maps autumn_wind
dislikes rats drizzle
fears a_shortcut_with_no_exit
hopes a_stall_worth_mapping
topics travel +0.5 pastimes +0.6 weather +0.3 land +0.2
styles comfort=walk gossip=dry refuse=wry tease=gentle
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# corrects old maps with little flights of steps and calculates how much wandering a direct errand can reasonably contain.

words
oath! = A gate drawn upside down | By my spare staircase
saying! = A straight road lacks useful corners | Fold a road and see what meets
chart = a much-folded plan | my creased chart
nib = my stub of chalk | a dry chalk end
turnoff = the crooked turning | a leftward kink
tread = the second tread | a shallow step
whiff = a little sour brine | the sharp fish smell
cove = a sheltered inlet | a bite in the shore
tray = a shallow tray | the oval service tray
crease = my diagonal fold | a corner crease
stall = a bit of awning | a narrow stall roof
gutter = a sunken gutter | the sloping channel
blow = a shoulder of wind | a tilt of wind
dot = a little hollow dot | one solid spot

any
opinion houses against 1 : An estate looks small enough on a map till you try going round it with an errand.
opinion merchants against 1 : If the chalked price has been rubbed off I don't like my chances of hearing a fair one aloud.
opinion sump for 1 : The low streets have more ways through than a surveying paw with clean boots might suppose.
opinion road for 2 : A walk with the time to lose a turning and find it again is my kind of day off.
opinion festivals for 1 : Give me a feast with a market at its centre and I can happily walk its circumference twice.
opinion watch against 1 : A grand uniform can stand right across a narrow stair and feel quite entitled to the spot.

grown
line greet : An agreeable interruption to my carefully crooked route. | Hello. I've contrived to arrive by the interesting way.
line greet [pair.band=strangers] : Our paths seem pleasantly unacquainted. | Welcome to this unremarkable point on my map.
line greet [here.time=dawn] : Morning. Everything looks more possible before the errands catch up. | Fresh light and an uncreased day to you.
line greet.return : Hello returned by the shortest available route. | I heard, even round that last turning of the talk.
line greet.return [pair.band=friends|family] : A friend's face ought to have its own mark on a map. | Excellent. A familiar landmark with ears.
line greet.return [here.time=night] : Late greetings, delivered somewhat circuitously. | A light in a window and a voice on the road. Welcome.
line again.open : Our routes have developed a resemblance again. | This corner appears to come furnished with your company.
line hail [pair.band=friends] : Walk the next little bend alongside me! | I've corrected a peculiar error. Come admire the map.
line farewell : An interesting road and a tolerable distance to you. | I hope the inconvenient turning proves handsome.
line farewell.return : I'll put another bend between us now. Goodbye. | May the next flight be short and regular.
line react.news : Tell it in whatever order the roads fall. | I'll fit the pieces together as we walk.
line react.news.new : My drawing has quite a blank space where that belongs. | New to me even in outline.
line react.news.known : Yes, that account followed me round an earlier corner. | I've seen the general shape of that already.
line react.news.doubt : That road appears to come out behind its own beginning. | A curious account. I'd want firmer ground halfway along.
line react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|crime|assault|loss|theft] : That's a cruel stretch to have to cover. Take my arm. | No pretty view makes that journey any shorter. I'm listening.
line react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|work] : That was worth going round three sides of a square to hear. | I'll take the pleasant way home in honour of such tidings.
line ask.how : Which way has the day been bending for you? | Been up more steps than down, or about even?
line answer.how : Somewhat footsore, with a fairly respectable view. | My legs object. My sense of direction remains untroubled.
line decline : I'd offer, but I should have to promise away tomorrow's legs as well. | That would put me on two roads at once. I'm sorry.
line accept_decline : We'll mark that way closed and look elsewhere. | I'll respect a clearly marked boundary.
line preclose : I should go. The walk back won't shorten itself. | I'm due a little distance before I sit.
line accept_preclose : Then off you go by the route that suits you. | We've reached a perfectly good turning place.
line thank : You've saved me the uninteresting half of the walk. Thank you. | I'm obliged. Consider that a favourable amendment to my map.
line deflect_thanks : A detour that short hardly merits a vote of thanks. | It was a welcome excuse to move my feet.
line sympathise : You may lean on me without explaining where you've been. | There's an unhurried way open for us if you'd like company.
line reassure : A wrong turn only tells us one thing about one road. | Rest your legs first. The map will keep.
line ack : That fits quite neatly at this turning. | I've found the place you're speaking of.
line give.advice : Draw the stairs as stairs or you'll be fooled in the dark. | Listen for running water before trusting a flat patch on a map.

scene blank_stairs
when topic=travel
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Look where this map says the road goes clean through a wall. | Here's a road with no earthly reason to exist in ink.
b : How does an actual walker manage? | What's actually there?
a : Up thirteen worn steps off to one side. I've put them back with chalk. | Steps standing on end. Whoever drew this saved a lot of climbing with one stroke.

scene wrong_map
when topic=pastimes self.likes=old_maps
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : My favourite maps need a little conversation to make sense. | A mildly inaccurate map provides an excellent afternoon.
b : Wouldn't an accurate one do? | How do you use the wrong ones?
a : For going somewhere, yes. For spending an afternoon I'd choose a mistake worth pursuing. | I walk to the error, then give the poor map a chance to explain itself.

scene wide_tread
when topic=travel
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : I like climbing in pairs of steps till somebody takes one out of the pattern. | An odd last tread always feels like an unpaid debt.
b : Your foot expects another one? | How do you account for a spare step?
a : Precisely. There hangs my knee, quite prepared to continue up the wall. | Mark it on my map and give my knee advance warning.

scene traytilt
when topic=work self.job=servant
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A tray makes a severe critic of a winding staircase. | I can go quite briskly round corners with my paws empty.
b : Why slower with plates? | What does a tray object to?
a : The turn at the top. A cup likes to finish a journey in the same direction it started. | Being asked to turn inside its own width. Very particular, crockery.

scene quiet_duty
when topic=work self.job=servant self.working=yes
does give.opinion / react.self / assess
a : An errand goes quicker if I read the room before I cross it. | I watch which way a door swings before filling my paws.
b : You plan for the return journey? | Got stuck in a doorway once?
a : The outward trip rarely involves a trayful of things nobody wants on the floor. | Let's just say I now admire doors that yield to a hip.

scene herring_way
when topic=food self.likes=pickled_herring
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A proper herring lunch ought to come with bread to mop the map afterwards. | Pickled fish and folded paper aren't natural travelling companions.
b : Wouldn't a plate do more good? | Spilled brine on a road?
a : It would. I can fold a map quite small. I've never been able to fold a plate. | A whole market square gained a tidal pool. Purely local event.

scene dry_drizzle
when topic=weather here.weather=rain
does tell.complaint / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Big drops announce a decision. Fine drizzle seems content to negotiate all afternoon. | This weather adds a grey margin to every route I take.
b : Can you walk round it? | Would you prefer a soaking?
a : Only on paper. My shoulders have been trying without success. | I'd prefer a dry day. Let's not give the sky any cheap ideas.

scene breeze_mark
when topic=weather self.likes=autumn_wind
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : In an autumn blow my map will turn a page without being asked. | I enjoy a gale. My papers enjoy it rather too freely.
b : Does it show the right street? | Ever lose a whole page?
a : It favours anywhere downwind. Sensible, if a little repetitive. | My most recent escapee turned up in a gutter. The new waterway it acquired is purely fanciful.

scene tact_spouse
when topic=family self.married=yes self.spouse
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd trust #self.spouse# with the map even on the day I admit it's wrong. | There's one person I'd quite enjoy getting lost with, namely #self.spouse#.
b : Even if you missed your dinner? | Wouldn't that lead to an argument?
a : I'd have my herring wrapped separately. There wouldn't be a crisis. | We could give the quarrel a name and put it down as a feature of the landscape.

scene hill_home
when topic=home self.quarter=sump
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A plan of the Sump is short on all the little climbs indoors. | Living where I do teaches you there's a great deal above a little square of ink.
b : You'd draw every storey? | How would you fit your stairs in?
a : Only if you'd lend me a sheet I could fold like a concertina. | An extra flap at each house. Lift it and discover how tired your legs ought to be.

scene futurestall
when topic=dreams
does tell.plan / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : My imaginary map includes a market stall with no name on it yet. | I'd like to draw myself a very small square under an awning one day.
b : Selling maps, I suppose? | What would you sell there?
a : I haven't settled that. Only the fact that the counter would be mine. | Something modest enough to accommodate a midday meal. I'm saving up for the decision.

scene unruly_rats
when topic=animals self.dislikes=rats
does tell.complaint / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A rat would read a map of my larder through an entrance behind the plaster. | I dislike the idea of my supper having a service entrance.
b : Got any entrances marked? | You mean little holes?
a : I've inked them out with plaster, where possible. Makes a persuasive map correction. | Doors, from the rat's point of view. I'd prefer a change of ownership.

scene gossip_walk
when topic=gossip
does give.opinion / react.self / assess
a : I like to send a hungry rumour the long way round. | A story that asks for directions to somebody else's kitchen can keep walking.
b : What directions would you give it? | Why not let it in?
a : Quite accurate ones to a dead end. It could use a little quiet there. | I prefer to choose the company my supper keeps.

scene lean_shoes
when topic=times world.times=lean|hard
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : If times worsen I'll draw my day's errands in a tighter spiral. | An orderly set of calls saves wear on tired shoes.
b : Is shoe leather really that dear? | Would you give up your detours?
a : Enough little journeys account for a whole sole. It never feels little at the cobbler's. | Only the uninteresting ones. I'm hard up for leather, not opinion.

scene festival_ink
when topic=festival
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Imagine drawing a festival map according to where the food smells strongest. | A festival deserves a different system of signs for one day.
b : A fish for the herring stalls? | What would indicate the musicians?
a : Exactly. No danger of mistaking lunch for a municipal building. | A wide flourish where the dancers need room. Carts may take the longer way.

scene price_room
when topic=prices
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A stall fee is a tidy way to charge rent on a patch of breeze. | I'm interested in the price of standing still with goods to sell.
b : What would make it worth paying? | Are you pricing the patch or the breeze?
a : Room to turn behind my counter and a fair stream of interested noses in front. | The patch. The breeze can pay rent wherever it blows to next.

scene chapel_step
when topic=faith
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : I like a chapel with a broad step at the door. | A moment on a chapel step does something for a long walk.
b : Praying for a shorter route? | Can't you go on inside?
a : I mean a longer breath. Even a short road improves after one. | Of course. Sometimes a moment by the door readies me for going in.

scene wrong_bay
when topic=land here.region=ridgemere
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : From a headland path the city on paper looks as if it might fit in a pocket. | Fold the city in four and the two headlands almost meet.
b : Would that shorten the trip round the bay? | You'd fold up the whole Sound?
a : On paper wonderfully. On foot I must still provide my own lunch. | In a dry pocket and at considerable risk to geography.

grown

story tray_route [topic=memories|work self.job=servant]
  : Drew a really efficient route for carrying empty dishes. Then I tried following it with a tray.
  : There was one door I'd given the useful power of swinging both ways. The real thing had scruples.
  b : Did the dishes survive?
  : Every one. My fine efficient route acquired a very inefficient backward dance.

story saltmap [topic=food|memories]
  : I marked a little square with a crumb while I ate. Afterwards I folded the plan and put it away.
  : Next time I opened it, the crumb had printed a market behind a blank stretch of hillside.
  b : Did it stay there?
  : I ate the original and rubbed out the copy. One meal had done quite enough town planning.

story slippers [topic=memories|travel]
  : I tested a short cut in my best shoes and had to walk the return way through an astonishing quantity of soaked grass.
  : Drew in a second little road alongside the first as soon as I got home.
  b : Did it acquire a name?
  : The road for any wolf intending to stay civil to the cobbler.

rule @mapmark
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 8h
say A stair has vanished off this page again. | Hold that corner down. The bay is folding over itself.

rule @tray
when concept=bark working=yes self.job=servant
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Give the tray the outside of the turn, please. | My elbows are ready to go round. The cups may differ.

rule @blow
when concept=bark here.weather=storm
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Fold quickly before the wind chooses our road. | There goes one corner of my little kingdom.

rule @wrong
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 8h
say I'll lend you my map after the hill's back in the right place. | One more turning and the drawing will agree with the stones.

dlg resident.hub : I can offer a little direction as long as you don't mind hearing about the other routes.
dlg resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #topic.player#, another crossing to add to my collection.
dlg resident.hub [here.time=night] : The roads are mostly shapes in the dark now. Talk is still quite legible.
dlg resident.hub [pair.disposition=wary|hostile] : I'd prefer to keep a whole pavement between our respective questions.
dlg resident.job [self.job=servant] : #self.trade_words.capitalize#. The most accomplished part is usually getting through a door with no paws free.
dlg resident.job : My work involves arriving when I'm needed despite several interesting opportunities to go astray.
dlg resident.bye : May the city's idea of a road agree with yours.

graft resident.hub
choice How do you draw steps on a flat map? -> drawingstairs
node drawingstairs
say Like the teeth in a comb. I make the last tooth crooked if the top tread is a different height. Saves passing feet a nasty surprise.
free
choice Do those marks make the map hard to read? -> toomanyteeth
choice I'll look for that crooked tooth. -> hub
node toomanyteeth
say As long as the streets outnumber the combs I call it a map. After that it's a warning to anybody considering a walk in that direction.
choice I'll consider my next turning. -> hub
choice Time I was on my way. -> bye
